From 54039b5c792c60a1bfa4067b45c5075a079da9d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 15:49:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06915/11362] [outer-loop] ls20: L6 SOLVED round 8 (codex,
 first attempt at fresh territory)

Round-8 gpt-5.6-sol session solved L6 on the first attempt. Two
blocking tuple targets in forced spatial order: an upper target must
be consumed before the lower one becomes reachable. Tuple controls are
moving collision objects (a shape-cycling shuttle, a rotation-cycling
shuttle, a color-cycling pinwheel) that only advance on valid player
movement. Mapped three fresh one-shot reset rings and both launchers.

Won live: set the upper target's tuple via the vertical launcher,
exited through the horizontal launcher, set the lower target's tuple
with a pinwheel-phase detour, and entered with 3 counter units to
spare. The source agent's own reproduction_verified is honestly false
(budget ran out after the win), but the outer loop independently
verified regardless: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via a new resolver
priority branch, all 5 confirmed level=6, state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED.

ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml: ls20 levels_reproduced 5 -> 6.
reproducible_total_levels 164 -> 165 (sum-checked;
arc_count_integrity_lint exit 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
